Dear list,

we again have some trouble with xenomai (x64 / 3.2.3 / ipipe /=20
linux 5.4.105): If we start a simple non-xenomai program while a xenomai=20
program running a thread in SCHED_FIFO (in our case prio 99) and getting=20
scheduled frequently, we sometimes (in our case with a probability of=20
0.2%) experience a segfault upon start of the simple program.

We reduced this case to a very simple xenomai app that endlessly runs a=20
loop with only nanosleep and a simple "hello world" non-xenomai app. The=20
sources of both you can find attached to this email, together with a=20
Makefile and a bash script that starts helloworld 1000000 times and=20
counts errors. Additionally you can find the config of our xenomai build=20
there.

We also experimented with xenomai versions a bit:
- xenomai 3.2.3 ipipe with linux 5.4.105 shows the problem
- xenomai 3.2.2 ipipe with linux 5.4.105 shows the problem
  =3D> it isn't a side effect of the patch you developed for us a while ago=
=20
  and that is included in 3.2.3
- xenomai 3.2.3 dovetail with linux 5.10.127 is clean.

Could you please have a look into that?

Best regards
Stefan

--_006_FR2P281MB2654953C4123B74DB77CDC51FCE0AFR2P281MB2654DEUP_
